Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An external review (2026-08-30) was analyzed claim by claim; each in-scope finding was probed
before being believed, and four were real:

- The P0: a reference that turns an INFERRED declaration into a value lost the list entirely.
  Reference expressions are typed before inference runs, so the completed declaration type never
  reaches them, and the side map was unioned for calls only — 'let w: () -> Unit = risky' with a
  throwing 'risky' compiled at 'error' and leaked at run time. The list is now demanded where the
  value is formed ('DemandInferredOnValue'), references are call-graph edges as "Recursion"
  requires ("its edges are calls and also references"), and the collecting pass picks the demand
  up, so a declaration that only references a thrower infers the requirement itself. Formation-
  site payment is stricter than the text's type-riding reading — the same boundary trade
  assumption imports made (artifact C15); declared clauses still ride the reference's type.
- A covered entry was still demanded: 'throws Base, Derived' demanded both. Call-site demands now
  pass through the semantic form ('NormalizeCapTys') — the list IS {Base}.
- An entry instantiated to an unchecked type did not vanish from the functional type for
  assignability: coverage now treats an unchecked sub-entry as trivially satisfied; the type
  manager learns the 'UncheckedException' root at type-check preparation. The entry still prints
  and still splits identity in invariant positions — recorded as I30, needs the CapList design.
- Effect capabilities were named 'Handler<C>' in diagnostics; the text defines 'CanPerform<C>'.

Plus one reconstruction site the review flagged: 'GetOriginalTy' rebuilt a functional type
without its capability list (and without its config flags); both are mapped through now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
